    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="9.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIIIAtr">VIII Atr</ref> 9.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="9.1" corresp="#wit-d">and eorðwestma be emnihte oððe huru be ealra halgena mæssan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="9[b]" corresp="#wit-d">and eorðwestma be emnihte, oððe huru be ealra halgena mæssan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d">And eorðwestma be emnihte oððe huru be Ealra Halgena mæssan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">and the tithe of the fruits of the earth by the equinox, or at least by the feast of All Saints.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d">And the tithe of the fruits of the earth by the equinox, or at least by the Feast of All Saints.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">und von Feldfrüchten zur Nachtgleiche oder wenigstens zum Aller-Heiligen-Fest.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">and of the fruits of the earth by the equinox, or at least by All Saints.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="265"><ref target="clause:IIEg_3">II Eg 3</ref>; <ref target="clause:VIAtr_17">VI Atr 17</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. VI Atr. 17</note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VI Atr 17.</note>
      </div>
